  "claim": "Ram Niwas Mirdha was chairman of a national level academy for performing arts. This is where the music composer of Daina (1984 film) won his award in 2008.",
  "evidencia": "Page: Bhupen Hazarika. Sentence: Recipient of Sangeet Natak Akademi Award (1987), Padmashri (1977), and Padmabhushan (2001), Hazarika was awarded with Dada Saheb Phalke Award (1992), India's highest award in cinema, by the Government of India and Sangeet Natak Akademi Fellowship (2008), the highest award of the Sangeet Natak Akademi, India's The National Academy for Music, Dance and Drama.\nPage: Sangeet Natak Akademi. Sentence: Sangeet Natak Akademi (Devanāgarī: \"संगीत नाटक अकादेमी\" or The National Academy for Music, Dance and Drama in English) is the national level academy for performing arts set up by the Government of India.\nPage: Daina (1984 film). Sentence: The music for the film is composed by Dr. Bhupen Hazarika.\nPage: Ram Niwas Mirdha. Sentence: He served as chairman of the Sangeet Natak Akademi until his death from multiple organ failure.",
