        "original_id": "afd3ba0e-94bf-5ecd-9804-32973ea3a633",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Bhupen Hazarika, Ram Niwas Mirdha\n- Organizations: Sangeet Natak Akademi, Government of India\n- Awards: Sangeet Natak Akademi Award, Padmashri, Dada Saheb Phalke Award, Padmabhushan, Sangeet Natak Akademi Fellowship\n- Works: Daina (1984 film)\n\nFacts:\n- In 1977, Bhupen Hazarika received the Padmashri.\n- In 1984, Dr. Bhupen Hazarika composed the music for the film Daina.\n- In 1987, Bhupen Hazarika received the Sangeet Natak Akademi Award.\n- In 1992, the Government of India awarded Bhupen Hazarika the Dada Saheb Phalke Award, India’s highest award in cinema.\n- In 2001, Bhupen Hazarika received the Padmabhushan.\n- In 2008, Bhupen Hazarika received the Sangeet Natak Akademi Fellowship, the highest award of the Sangeet Natak Akademi.\n- Sangeet Natak Akademi is the national-level academy for performing arts set up by the Government of India.\n- Sangeet Natak Akademi is The National Academy for Music, Dance and Drama in English.\n- Ram Niwas Mirdha served as chairman of the Sangeet Natak Akademi until his death from multiple organ failure.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
